   \[
   \text{Loading dose} = \text{Dose per kg} \times \text{Weight in kg} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.5 \text{ kg} = 280 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the infusion time in minutes**:
   \[
   \text{Infusion time} = \frac{\text{Loading dose}}{\text{Infusion rate}} = \frac{280 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 56 \text{ min}
   \]

