   \Delta S_{CO} = 100.0 \text{ J/mol·K}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta S_{CO_2} = 100.0 \text{ J/mol·K}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta S_{O_2} = 100.0 \text{ J/mol·K}
   \]
   Substituting:
   \[
   \Delta S = 3(100.0) - 3(100.0) - 1.5(100.0) = 300 - 300 - 150 = -150 \text{ J/K}
   \]

5. **Alternative method using Gibbs law:**
   \[
   \Delta S = \frac{\Delta H}{T} = \frac{-3400}{298} = -11.1 \text{ J/K}
   \]

The correct answer is:
\[
\Delta S = -150 \text{ J/K}
