The reaction between benzoic acid (H(C₇H₅O₂)) and sodium hydroxide (NaOH) can be represented as follows:

\[
\text{H}_2\text{C₇H₅O}_2(s] + \text{NaOH}(aq] \rightarrow \text{H}_2\text{C₇H}_5\text{OH}^- + \text{Na}^ + \rightarrow \text{H}_2\text{C₇H}_5\text{OH}^- + \text{Na}^ +
\]

**Explanation:**
