   - Isotopomers are chemically distinct isomers of a molecule that differ only in the number of atoms of a specific isotope.
   - Isotopomers are formed when a molecule has multiple hydrogen atoms (or other isotopes like ¹¹C, ¹³C, or ¹⁴N).
