For the first term, \( 3\sin\leftleft(\frac{2x + \pi/4\right) \), the first term is \( 3 \), which is the scaling factor. The inner term is \( \frac{2x + \pi/4} \), so the base term is \( 2x \). The period of \( \sin( 2x \) is \( \frac{2\pi}{2} = pi \). Thus, the period of \( 3\sin\leftleft(\frac{2x + \pi/4}\right) \) is \( \pi \).

