<start_of_turn>model
","For an isothermal expansion of an ideal gas, the work done is given by the formula:  
\[
P_1 \times \Delta V = \text{Work \text{ done}}
\]  
where \( P_1 \) is the initial pressure and \( \Delta V \) is the change in volume.  

Given:  
- Initial pressure \( P_1 = 2 \, \text{atm} \)  
- Initial volume \( V_1 = 4 \, \text{L} \)  
- Final volume \( V_2 = 8 \, \text{L} \)  

The change in volume is:  
\[
\Delta V = V_2 - V_1 = 8 \, \text{L} - 4 \, \text{L} = 4 \, \text{L}
\]  

Thus, the work done is:  
\[
W = P_1 \cdot \Delta V = 2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L} = 8 \, \text{J}
\]  

Thus, the work done by the gas during the expansion process is \(\boxed{8 \, \text{J}}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
