   - Cylinder B: \( A_B = \frac{2 \times \sqrt{2} \times 25 \text{ mm}}{3} = \frac{2 \times 0.025 \text{ m}}{3} = 0.00833 \text{ m}^2 \)

2. **Calculate the weight of the piston:**
   \[ W = m g = 25 \text{ kg} \times 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 = 245.15 \text{ N} \]

3. **Apply the equilibrium equation:**
   The pressure in cylinder A (P_A) must balance the pressure in cylinder B (P_B), the weight of the piston (W), and the atmospheric pressure (P_atm).
   \[ P_A = P_B + W/A_B + P_{atm} \]
